WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.637
PIV is the one part the
migration doesn't re-issue.

2
00:00:03.637 --> 00:00:08.200
Those certificates still come from the
Federal PKI through the card system.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.331
What changes is who trusts them: the federal
root has to reach devices and servers,

4
00:00:13.331 --> 00:00:17.313
and Entra ID has to check each
card against its revocation list.

5
00:00:17.313 --> 00:00:18.699
Two choices matter.

6
00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:22.874
Every authority Entra trusts can
sign in any user it's bound to,

7
00:00:22.874 --> 00:00:24.838
so bindings have to be strong.

8
00:00:24.838 --> 00:00:27.711
And a PIN-protected card
counts as multifactor,

9
00:00:27.711 --> 00:00:32.649
while a software certificate doesn't, so
derived credentials need their own rule.

10
00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:37.041
The decision for the CISO: require
high-affinity bindings in production,

11
00:00:37.041 --> 00:00:40.712
and send any weaker binding kept
to the authorizing official.

12
00:00:40.712 --> 00:00:42.410
So who owns all of this?
